From: Cleo <ai.ops@atomixlogistics.com>
To: Drake <Drake@atomixlogistics.com>
Subject: TEST — Combined Ops CX Finance Morning Meeting — 2026-06-12

<#multipart type=alternative>
<#part type=text/plain>
Good morning team.

Here are the three things I learned yesterday that can help Atomix today:

1. Early communication protects trust. If a delay, missing document, or billing issue might touch the client, the first win is communicating before they have to ask.
2. Clean handoffs reduce repeat work. Ops, CX, and Finance need one owner, one status, and one next action on every open issue.
3. Margin protection starts in the details. Detention, accessorials, labor waste, and unresolved tickets are small leaks until they repeat.

Attached is the combined Ops, CX, and Finance morning meeting agenda. For this test, use this link:

Combined agenda: https://drake-arch.github.io/atomix-ops/morning_agendas/2026-06-12-test/combined.html

We do what we say, and if we can't, we communicate early.

