body{background:#eef1f4}.email{max-width:860px;margin:32px auto;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e5e7eb;border-radius:16px;padding:34px;box-shadow:0 8px 30px rgba(15,23,42,.12)}.email h1{font-size:30px;margin:0 0 16px}.email p,.email li{font-size:17px;line-height:1.55;color:#52627a}.email ol{padding-left:24px}.links{display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:22px 0}.sig{font-weight:900;color:#07152a;font-size:19px;margin-top:28px}</style></head><body><main class="email"><h1>Good morning team.</h1><p>Here are the three things I learned yesterday that can help Atomix today:</p><ol><li><strong>Early communication protects trust.</strong> If a delay, missing document, or billing issue might touch the client, the first win is communicating before they have to ask.</li><li><strong>Clean handoffs reduce repeat work.</strong> Ops, CX, and Finance need one owner, one status, and one next action on every open issue.</li><li><strong>Margin protection starts in the details.</strong> Detention, accessorials, labor waste, and unresolved tickets are small leaks until they repeat.</li></ol><p>Attached is the combined Ops, CX, and Finance morning meeting agenda. For this test, use the link below:</p><div class="links"><a class="btn" href="https://drake-arch.github.io/atomix-ops/morning_agendas/2026-06-12-test/combined.html">Open Combined Morning Meeting Agenda</a></div><p class="sig">We do what we say, and if we can't, we communicate early.</p><p class="meta">Test email preview · fake CX/Finance data · Ops agenda from today copied into this combined meeting deck.</p></main></body></html>
